{"name":"Cement","hex":"#a5a391","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Cement","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A town in Oklahoma."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Cement"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cement","blocks":[{"text":"A cement is a binder used for construction that sets, hardens, and adheres to other materials to bind them together. Cement is seldom used on its own, but rather to bind sand and gravel (aggregate) together. Cement mixed with fine aggregate produces mortar for masonry, or with sand and gravel, produces concrete. Concrete is the most widely used material in existence and is behind only water as the planet's most-consumed resource."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/USMC-110806-M-IX060-148.jpg/330px-USMC-110806-M-IX060-148.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cement","wikidata":"Q45190"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/LDClinkerScaled.jpg/500px-LDClinkerScaled.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/LDClinkerScaled.jpg/500px-LDClinkerScaled.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Clinker nodules produced by sintering at 1450 °C","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALDClinkerScaled.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Calcium_oxide_powder.JPG/500px-Calcium_oxide_powder.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Calcium_oxide_powder.JPG/1280px-Calcium_oxide_powder.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Calcium_oxide_powder.JPG/500px-Calcium_oxide_powder.JPG?utm_source=